  "raw": {
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3260": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist CL2 - Athletics",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Department: UMF Athletics Category: Administrative Support JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Farmington, ME, United States Peacefully nestled in the spectacular lakes & mountains region of western Maine, UMF is Maine’s public liberal arts college, offering quality programs in teacher education, human services and arts and sciences. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. University of Maine at Farmington Are you ready to be the ultimate playmaker behind the scenes? Every great athletic department needs a central powerhouse to keep the team moving, and that is exactly what our Administrative Specialist does. As the sole administrative support anchor for our entire athletics department, you will be the driving force connecting sports teams, coaches, sports medicine, compliance, sports information, and our campus. If you thrive in a dynamic, high-energy environment, love sports culture, and pride yourself on keeping multiple moving pieces perfectly synchronized, this is your invitation to join our roster. From coordination to game-day logistics, your work will directly impact the success of our student-athletes and staff. Your Game Plan (sample of responsiblities) The Face of the Franchise: Deliver championship-level front-facing customer service by answering inquiries, and welcoming students, faculty, staff and the community to the campus. Logistics Coordinator: Keep our teams moving by arranging travel and reservations for away games, processing home and away athletic contracts, and cross-checking schedules. Master of Facilities: Direct traffic for our athletic venues by managing and prioritizing scheduling requests for Dearborn Gym, the Prescott Athletic Complex, and Leib Field. You will even coordinate reservations for fun department equipment, like portable speakers and our mascot costume! Financial Game Planner: Handle basic accounts payable and receivable across varsity programs, fundraising accounts, and sports medicine. You will track, monitor, and report on balances, process vendor payments, and deposit game-day gate and entry fees. Team Captain for Operations: Oversee student workers assigned to office work, facility monitoring, and event setups. You will also assist with onboarding new staff and independent contractors (like game officials and assignors). Special Events Producer: Provide hands-on coordination and planning support for major department highlights, including the Hall of Fame, athletic championships, recruitment nights, and alumni fundraisers. What You Bring to the Roster Education & Experience: A high school diploma or equivalent (G.E.D.) paired with 1+ years of administrative support experience. Communication MVPs: Excellent customer service skills with the ability to handle communication professionally across many channels, even in a bustling environment with frequent interruptions. Tech Savvy: Strong computer proficiency, particularly with spreadsheets, data tracking, and digital organization tools. Integrity & Trust: Absolute discretion and the ability to securely handle confidential student-athlete, faculty, and institutional information. Adaptability: The judgment, initiative, and team-first attitude required to balance routine bookkeeping with sudden game-day adjustments. The starting rate is $20.39 for a new hire or the appropriate transfer rate for a current employee within the ACSUM collective bargaining unit. In addition, the University will contribute up to a 4% matching contribution to the UMS retirement plan. The University of Maine at Farmington offers a highly competitive benefits that includes holiday and sick time, medical, dental, and vision insurance, life insurance, short- and long-term disability insurance, a tuition waiver program for employees and eligible dependents, retirement plan options, and more. Visit our benefits website to learn more. Job Description Application Requirements: Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact information for three (3) professional references Important items to know about the recruitment process: For full consideration, materials must be submitted by 4:30 pm EST Friday, October 23, 2026 We are not able to consider applicants who require Visa sponsorship. Incomplete recruitment materials will not be considered. If materials are received after the recruitment deadline, review will be at the discretion of the University. The successful applicant is subject to appropriate background screenings. The University of Maine at Farmington employees are Mandatory Reporters with the exception of UMF’s licensed, clinical medical providers (including athletic trainers) and mental health providers and their clinical interns when working in their capacity as providers. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix /. Clery Act The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish, and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report . If you wish to have a paper copy of the ASR or you need to have a copy of the ASR in an accessible format, the University will provide such a copy upon request. Please contact: UMF Department of Public Safety / Campus Police, University of Maine at Farmington, 149 Quebec Street, Farmington, Maine 04938-1994, tel 207-778-7400. The University of Maine at Farmington has earned a national reputation for excellence, gaining stature as one of the finest state-supported liberal arts colleges in the northeastern U.S. Additionally, UMF is rated 5th in U.S. News & World Report Top Regional Public College North for 2023 and has been rated one of America's Best Colleges by U.S. News 25 times since 1998. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. With enrollment at around 1,600 full-time students, UMF is about the same size as many of New England’s most selective private colleges and offers many of the same advantages, yet at a very affordable price — providing a tremendous college value in a spectacular natural setting. Established in 1864 as Maine’s first public institution of higher education, the University of Maine at Farmington is a founding member of The Council of Public Liberal Arts Colleges (COPLAC) an exclusive national group of public colleges and universities committed to providing superior liberal arts and sciences education. "
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3261": {
      "title": "Career Advisor & Outdoor Recreation Hub Coordinator",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Department: UMF Learning Assistance Center Category: Student Life Services JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Farmington, ME, United States Peacefully nestled in the spectacular lakes & mountains region of western Maine, UMF is Maine’s public liberal arts college, offering quality programs in teacher education, human services and arts and sciences. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. The University of Maine Farmington(UMF) is looking for a high-energy, visionary leader to step into a dual-impact role as our Career Advisor & Outdoor Recreation HUB Coordinator . Maine's outdoor recreation economy isn't just a sector - it's a billion-dollar powerhouse and the beating heart of our state's identity. At UMF, we don't just hand out degrees; we forge the trailblazers who will lead this vital industry into the future. In this hybrid position, you are the ultimate bridge-builder. You'll stand at the intersection of academic theory and real-world adventure, turning student potential into professional excellence. Based on the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant, the anticipated annual salary is $46,911 plus a 10% employer contribution to the UMS retirement plan. Additional benefits include medical, dental, vision, and tuition waiver programs for employees and dependents. Key Responsibilities Strategic Career Mentorship Pathway Advising: Act as a dedicated mentor for students in outdoor recreation, hospitality, and tourism, helping them navigate career expropriation and professional identity. Skill Translation: Provide expert guidance on resume development and interview preparation, specifically helping students translate “field experience” into professional assets. Workshop & Education: Design and lead seminars on job search strategies and evolving trends of the recreation industry. Industry Partnership & HUB Coordination Economic Liaison: Build high-level partnerships with Maine's business, government, and non-profit sectors to secure internships and sustainable career pipelines. Experiential Learning: Work with faculty to ensure that classroom learning is matched with “hands-on” field opportunities. Event Architecture: Organize guest speaker series, industry networking nights, and student-led professional initiatives. System Integration: Collaborate with the University of Maine System (UMS) to align regional goals and share industry resources. Required Skills & Core Competencies Strategic Planning & Organization: Proven ability to plan and organize complex workflows, managing time effectively to accomplish diverse job duties. Innovative Problem Solving: Ability to utilize existing and emerging tools to create innovative approaches to challenges and develop new opportunities within the outdoor recreation and hospitality sectors. Analytical Evaluation: Excellent skill set in observing and evaluating the outcomes of implemented solutions; demonstrated ability to pivot and implement alternative approaches based on lessons learned. Stakeholder Communication: Outstanding interpersonal, written, verbal, and presentation skills, with a demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with all university and industry stakeholders. Leadership & Collaboration: A collaborative work style with proven leadership across all levels of employees and a commitment to maintaining confidentiality with sensitive information. Adaptability: The ability to react positively and effectively to change and a rapidly evolving campus focus. Principled Judgement: Demonstrated ability to make ethical decisions and exercise principled judgement with a high level of attention to detail. Technological Proficiency: Advanced knowledge of and ability to use institutional technology, including PeopleSoft (MainStreet), Concur, Microsoft Office Suite, Google Suite, and Zoom. Student Development Foundations: Solid understanding of the sound principles of student development and their application in a higher education setting. Career Development Expertise: Foundational knowledge of career development theories, labor force data, and career resources. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree in Career Services, Student Affairs, Outdoor Recreation, Business, or a related field. Professional Experience: Four (4) to six (6) years of professional related experience in career services or student affairs, which must include at least three (3) years specifically within the outdoor recreation, hospitality, or tourism industries. Mentorship: Direct experience advising and/or mentoring students or young professionals. Program Development: Demonstrated experience developing internship programs and building successful relationships with employers. Preferred Qualifications Industry Insight: Advanced knowledge of current job trends within Maine and the regional New England economy. External Relations: Strong public relations and networking experience with a track record of building industry-wide connections. Institutional Knowledge: A thorough understanding of the principles of college student development and the specific policies and structures of a four-year public university system. Given the specialized nature of this role, we encourage applications from Veterans with professional backgrounds in MWR Program Management, Career Counseling and Personnel Officers, or Command and Logistics Leadership. Full Job Description Application Requirements: Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Candidates selected to proceed to the final stages of the search process will be requested to provide a list of references. Important information: We are not able to consider applicants who require any visa sponsorship support Incomplete application materials cannot be considered. Materials received after the initial review date will be reviewed at the discretion of the University. For full consideration, materials must be submitted by 4:30 pm EST on Friday, October 30, 2026 The successful applicant is subject to appropriate background screening. The University of Maine at Farmington employees are Mandatory Reporters with the exception of UMF’s licensed, clinical medical providers (including athletic trainers), and mental health providers and their clinical interns when working in their capacity as providers. . Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/ . Clery Act The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report . If you have any questions, contact UMF Dept. of Public, Safety / Campus Police, University of Maine at Farmington, 149 Quebec Street, Farmington, Maine 04938-1994 tel 207-778-7400UMF The University of Maine at Farmington has earned a national reputation for excellence, gaining stature as one of the finest state-supported liberal arts colleges in the northeastern U.S. Additionally, UMF is rated 5th in U.S. News & World Report Top Regional Public College North for 2023 and has been rated one of America's Best Colleges by U.S. News 25 times since 1998. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. With enrollment at around 1,600 full-time students, UMF is about the same size as many of New England’s most selective private colleges and offers many of the same advantages, yet at a very affordable price — providing a tremendous college value in a spectacular natural setting. Established in 1864 as Maine’s first public institution of higher education, the University of Maine at Farmington is a founding member of The Council of Public Liberal Arts Colleges (COPLAC) an exclusive national group of public colleges and universities committed to providing superior liberal arts and sciences education. "
