    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3253": {
      "title": "Grants and Contracts Manager",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Department: UMF VP for Administration Category: Fiscal,Finance and Business JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Farmington, ME, United States Peacefully nestled in the spectacular lakes & mountains region of western Maine, UMF is Maine’s public liberal arts college, offering quality programs in teacher education, human services and arts and sciences. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. Are you a skilled financial professional who enjoys turning complex grant requirements into clear, practical solutions? The University of Maine at Farmington (UMF) is seeking a Grants and Contracts Manager to provide financial leadership, compliance oversight, and stewardship for UMF’s sponsored programs portfolio. Reporting to the Director of Finance, this position manages the financial lifecycle of approximately $14 million in externally funded grants and contracts, from proposal development and award setup through ongoing administration, reporting, audit, and final closeout. This is an excellent opportunity for someone who combines strong financial and analytical skills with a collaborative approach and enjoys helping faculty, staff, and project leaders successfully navigate the world of sponsored funding. What You’ll Do Manage Sponsored Funding: Direct the financial administration of UMF’s grants and contracts throughout the full award lifecycle, including proposal budgets, award setup, amendments, invoicing, reporting, audits, and closeout. Be a Trusted Resource: Partner with principal investigators, project leaders, department budget managers, sponsors, auditors, and University System offices to provide guidance and support successful project outcomes. Strengthen Compliance: Provide guidance on Uniform Guidance, allowable costs, sponsor requirements, University policies, procurement, payroll, subawards, record retention, and related compliance matters. Turn Data into Action: Analyze proposals and risk indicators and develop actionable recommendations for University leadership, principal investigators, and budget managers. Improve How We Work: Evaluate grants management processes and financial systems and lead improvements that strengthen controls, improve data quality, reduce manual work, and increase efficiency. Build Knowledge Across Campus: Develop training, tools, and guidance to strengthen grants management practices and help faculty and staff successfully administer sponsored funding. Job Description Based on the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant, the annual salary range for this position is $54,000 - $58,000 plus a 10% employer contribution to the UMS retirement plan. Additional benefits include medical, dental, vision, and tuition waiver programs for employees and dependents. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in accounting, finance, business administration, economics, or a closely related field. Minimum of three years of progressively responsible professional experience in grants administration, sponsored programs, accounting, finance, or a related financial field. Experience administering grants or contracts, including post-award financial management and compliance with sponsor requirements. Working knowledge of budgeting, accounting, internal controls, and financial reporting within a complex organization. Proficiency with spreadsheets and financial reporting tools, including formulas, queries, pivot tables, data validation, reconciliations, and financial modeling. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in accounting, finance, business administration, public administration, or a related field. Certified Research Administrator (CRA), Certified Public Accountant (CPA), Certified Management Accountant (CMA), or other relevant professional credentials. Experience in higher education, governmental accounting, or public sector financial management. Experience with PeopleSoft Financials, Concur, grants management systems, or comparable enterprise financial systems. Why UMF? At UMF, the Grants and Contracts Manager is more than a financial administrator. You’ll serve as a trusted advisor and collaborative partner , helping ensure sponsored funds are managed accurately and responsibly while developing practices and processes that support the University’s academic and institutional mission. Application Requirements: Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact information for three (3) professional references We are not able to consider applicants who require any visa sponsorship support Incomplete application materials cannot be considered. Materials received after the initial review date will be reviewed at the discretion of the University. For full consideration, materials must be submitted by 4:30 pm EST Tuesday, October 27, 2026 The successful applicant is subject to appropriate background screening and post-offer physical as applicable. The University of Maine at Farmington employees are Mandatory Reporters with the exception of UMF’s licensed, clinical medical providers (including athletic trainers) and mental health providers and their clinical interns when working in their capacity as providers. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/ . Clery Act The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report . If you have any questions, contact UMF Dept. of Public, Safety / Campus Police, University of Maine at Farmington, 149 Quebec Street, Farmington, Maine 04938-1994 tel 207-778-7400UMF The University of Maine at Farmington has earned a national reputation for excellence, gaining stature as one of the finest state-supported liberal arts colleges in the northeastern U.S. Additionally, UMF is rated 5th in U.S. News & World Report Top Regional Public College North for 2023 and has been rated one of America's Best Colleges by U.S. News 25 times since 1998. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. With enrollment at around 1,600 full-time students, UMF is about the same size as many of New England’s most selective private colleges and offers many of the same advantages, yet at a very affordable price — providing a tremendous college value in a spectacular natural setting. Established in 1864 as Maine’s first public institution of higher education, the University of Maine at Farmington is a founding member of The Council of Public Liberal Arts Colleges (COPLAC) an exclusive national group of public colleges and universities committed to providing superior liberal arts and sciences education. "
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3254": {
      "title": "Emerging Technology Coordinator",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Department: UMF Inst Tech Support Services Category: Information Technology [Sa1] JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Farmington, ME, United States Peacefully nestled in the spectacular lakes & mountains region of western Maine, UMF is Maine’s public liberal arts college, offering quality programs in teacher education, human services and arts and sciences. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. Help shape the future of Emerging Technology at UMF The University of Maine at Farmington is seeking an innovative, collaborative, and forward-thinking Emerging Technology Coordinator to lead our campus-wide efforts in exploring, evaluating, and thoughtfully adopting new technology, from AI to the next tools on the horizon. This is an exciting opportunity for someone who enjoys exploring what’s next, and helping others turn new technology into meaningful opportunities. You’ll serve as a central resource for emerging technologies at UMF, partnering with faculty, staff, students, and campus leaders to build digital and AI literacy, support innovative teaching and learning, and help the University navigate a rapidly changing technological landscape. What You’ll Do: You’ll help move UMF from “What can this technology do?” to “How can we use it thoughtfully and effectively?” Your work will include: Leading campus efforts to identify and evaluate emerging technologies including AI and responsible-use practices. Creating engaging training and related professional development on these new technologies for faculty, staff, and students. Working one-on-one with faculty to explore effective practices in the use of emerging technologies, including in areas such as AI-supported course design and alternative assessments. Partnering with the Library to strengthen AI and information literacy across campus. Exploring and evaluating innovative tools and projects, including chatbots, agents, rapid prototyping, and other emerging learning technologies. Based on the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant, the annual salary for this position is up to $60,000 plus a 10% employer contribution to the UMS retirement plan. Additional benefits include medical, dental, vision, and tuition waiver programs for employees and dependents. Job Description Required Qualifications: Master's degree in education, technology, instructional design, learning sciences, or a related field and a minimum of one (1) year of direct hands-on experience designing, piloting, or evaluating AI-based tools or workflows in an educational or professional context, or a combination of education and experience to equate to a total of 6 years. Demonstrated and documented enthusiasm for exploring how AI can responsibly enhance teaching and learning, balanced with critical judgment about its limitations and ethical risks. Demonstrated and documented collaboration and consultation skills, including experience working across multiple constituencies in a professional setting. Demonstrated and documented initiative, project coordination skills, and a service-oriented attitude. Preferred Qualifications: Experience co-authoring or supporting external grant applications. Experience designing and facilitating professional development or training programs at scale (workshops, cohort-based programs, communities of practice) for varied audiences, including students and staff. Working knowledge of data privacy, copyright, and accessibility considerations (including Title II) as they apply to AI and instructional technology tools. Understanding of learning theories, instructional design methods, and learner-centered design principles. Application Requirements: Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact information for three (3) professional references We are not able to consider applicants who require any visa sponsorship support Incomplete application materials cannot be considered. Materials received after the initial review date will be reviewed at the discretion of the University. For full consideration, materials must be submitted by 4:30 pm EST Tuesday, October 27, 2026 The successful applicant is subject to appropriate background screening and post-offer physical as applicable. The University of Maine at Farmington employees are Mandatory Reporters with the exception of UMF’s licensed, clinical medical providers (including athletic trainers) and mental health providers and their clinical interns when working in their capacity as providers. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/ . Clery Act The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report . If you have any questions, contact UMF Dept. of Public, Safety / Campus Police, University of Maine at Farmington, 149 Quebec Street, Farmington, Maine 04938-1994 tel 207-778-7400UMF The University of Maine at Farmington has earned a national reputation for excellence, gaining stature as one of the finest state-supported liberal arts colleges in the northeastern U.S. Additionally, UMF is rated 5th in U.S. News & World Report Top Regional Public College North for 2023 and has been rated one of America's Best Colleges by U.S. News 25 times since 1998. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. With enrollment at around 1,600 full-time students, UMF is about the same size as many of New England’s most selective private colleges and offers many of the same advantages, yet at a very affordable price — providing a tremendous college value in a spectacular natural setting. Established in 1864 as Maine’s first public institution of higher education, the University of Maine at Farmington is a founding member of The Council of Public Liberal Arts Colleges (COPLAC) an exclusive national group of public colleges and universities committed to providing superior liberal arts and sciences education. "
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3204": {
      "title": "Retail Services Supervisor",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/10/2026 Department: UMF Bookstore Category: Retail Operations JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Farmington, ME, United States Peacefully nestled in the spectacular lakes & mountains region of western Maine, UMF is Maine’s public liberal arts college, offering quality programs in teacher education, human services and arts and sciences. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. Are you an experienced retail professional who enjoys leading a team, providing exceptional customer service, and keeping operations running smoothly? The University of Maine at Farmington is seeking a Retail Services Supervisor to provide essential professional oversight for the University Store, Mailroom, and campus Card Services. This auxiliary position combines hands-on leadership with responsibility for key day-to-day operations. Beyond supervising, scheduling, training, and managing student staff, the Retail Services Supervisor helps ensure efficient and customer-focused services across these important campus operations. The position oversees retail activities, textbook ordering and returns, inventory and merchandise displays, online orders, financial records and transactions, and special events and sales. The successful candidate will be a strong team leader who can prioritize competing responsibilities, resolve complex customer and student needs, maintain accurate operational and financial records, and model excellent customer service. Qualifications Six months of specialized training or education beyond high school. Three years of retail experience. One year of supervisory or lead-level experience. Additional qualifying experience may substitute for the required education. Demonstrated knowledge and skills in customer service, supervision, scheduling, merchandising, retail operations, and related financial practices. Starting Salary: $20.39 per hour If you are a customer-focused who enjoys leading others and contributing to services that support students, employees, and the broader campus community, we invite you to apply and join the UMF team! Job Description The University of Maine at Farmington offers a highly competitive benefits package that includes holiday and sick time, medical, dental, and vision insurance, life insurance, short- and long-term disability insurance, a tuition waiver program for employees and eligible dependents, retirement plan options, and more. Visit our benefits website to learn more. The University of Maine at Farmington employees are Mandatory Reporters with the exception of UMF’s licensed, clinical medical providers (including athletic trainers), and mental health providers and their clinical interns when working in their capacity as providers. Important items to know about the recruitment process: Review of applications will begin following the end of business on Friday, October 16, 2026 We are not able to consider applicants who require Visa sponsorship. Incomplete recruitment materials will not be considered. If materials are received after the recruitment deadline, review will be at the discretion of the University. The successful applicant is subject to appropriate background screenings. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix /. The University of Maine at Farmington employees are Mandatory Reporters with the exception of UMF’s licensed, clinical medical providers (including athletic trainers), and mental health providers and their clinical interns when working in their capacity as providers. Clery Act The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish, and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report . If you wish to have a paper copy of the ASR or you need to have a copy of the ASR in an accessible format, the University will provide such a copy upon request. Please contact: UMF Department of Public Safety / Campus Police, University of Maine at Farmington, 149 Quebec Street, Farmington, Maine 04938-1994, tel 207-778-7400. The University of Maine at Farmington has earned a national reputation for excellence, gaining stature as one of the finest state-supported liberal arts colleges in the northeastern U.S. Additionally, UMF is rated 5th in U.S. News & World Report Top Regional Public College North for 2023 and has been rated one of America's Best Colleges by U.S. News 25 times since 1998. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. With enrollment at around 1,600 full-time students, UMF is about the same size as many of New England’s most selective private colleges and offers many of the same advantages, yet at a very affordable price — providing a tremendous college value in a spectacular natural setting. Established in 1864 as Maine’s first public institution of higher education, the University of Maine at Farmington is a founding member of The Council of Public Liberal Arts Colleges (COPLAC) an exclusive national group of public colleges and universities committed to providing superior liberal arts and sciences education. "
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3225": {
      "title": "Accounting Support Specialist CL2",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/10/2026 Department: UMF Administrative Systems Category: Accounting Support JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Farmington, ME, United States Peacefully nestled in the spectacular lakes & mountains region of western Maine, UMF is Maine’s public liberal arts college, offering quality programs in teacher education, human services and arts and sciences. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. Put your eye for detail and financial know-how to work supporting Maine’s public universities. The University of Maine System is seeking an Accounting Support Specialist to join its team. This position is ideal for someone who enjoys working with numbers, solving problems, keeping financial information organized and accurate, and providing excellent service to others. Accounting Support Specialists play an important role in the receipt, disbursement, tracking, and review of financial information. Responsibilities may range from financial data entry and transaction processing to account reconciliation, budget monitoring, financial reporting, and other accounting support activities. What You’ll Do In this role, you may: Support accounts payable and accounts receivable, including reviewing accounts, processing invoices and financial forms, and preparing fiscal information. Process and reconcile financial transactions, deposits, cash and non-cash transactions. Communicate with vendors, customers, students, and university departments to answer questions and help resolve payment, billing, and account issues. Monitor budget activity and assist with general ledger reconciliation, journal entries, reporting, and budget preparation. Process payroll-related activities and maintain accurate financial documentation. Use computerized systems for financial data entry, research, reconciliation, and reporting. Depending on the career level, research discrepancies, audit accounts, generate financial reports, assist with account reconciliation and year-end accounting activities, and support increasingly complex financial matters. What We’re Looking For We’re looking for someone who brings accuracy, organization, sound judgment, strong customer service, and the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. The position requires skills in balancing and recording transactions, monitoring accounts, maintaining records, querying data, preparing reports, and communicating effectively with coworkers, students, supervisors, administration and potentially the public. If you are detail-oriented, comfortable working with financial information, committed to accuracy, and enjoy helping others, this is an opportunity to put those strengths to work in support of the University community. Bring your attention to detail, problem-solving skills, and commitment to great service to Maine’s public universities—we encourage you to apply! Starting Wage: $20.39 per hour Job Description Qualifications High school diploma or GED and two years of accounting support experience. Additional qualifying experience may substitute for the education required for the assigned position. The University of Maine at Farmington offers a highly competitive benefits package that includes holiday and sick time, medical, dental, and vision insurance, life insurance, short- and long-term disability insurance, a tuition waiver program for employees and eligible dependents, retirement plan options, and more. Visit our benefits website to learn more. The University of Maine at Farmington employees are Mandatory Reporters with the exception of UMF’s licensed, clinical medical providers (including athletic trainers), and mental health providers and their clinical interns when working in their capacity as providers. Important items to know about the recruitment process: Review of applications will begin on following the end of business on Friday, October 16, 2026 We are not able to consider applicants who require Visa sponsorship. Incomplete recruitment materials will not be considered. If materials are received after the recruitment deadline, review will be at the discretion of the University. The successful applicant is subject to appropriate background screenings. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix /. The University of Maine at Farmington employees are Mandatory Reporters with the exception of UMF’s licensed, clinical medical providers (including athletic trainers), and mental health providers and their clinical interns when working in their capacity as providers. Clery Act The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish, and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report . If you wish to have a paper copy of the ASR or you need to have a copy of the ASR in an accessible format, the University will provide such a copy upon request. Please contact: UMF Department of Public Safety / Campus Police, University of Maine at Farmington, 149 Quebec Street, Farmington, Maine 04938-1994, tel 207-778-7400. The University of Maine at Farmington has earned a national reputation for excellence, gaining stature as one of the finest state-supported liberal arts colleges in the northeastern U.S. Additionally, UMF is rated 5th in U.S. News & World Report Top Regional Public College North for 2023 and has been rated one of America's Best Colleges by U.S. News 25 times since 1998. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. With enrollment at around 1,600 full-time students, UMF is about the same size as many of New England’s most selective private colleges and offers many of the same advantages, yet at a very affordable price — providing a tremendous college value in a spectacular natural setting. Established in 1864 as Maine’s first public institution of higher education, the University of Maine at Farmington is a founding member of The Council of Public Liberal Arts Colleges (COPLAC) an exclusive national group of public colleges and universities committed to providing superior liberal arts and sciences education. "
