    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3233": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach M/W Alpine",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/10/2026 Department: UMF Athletics Category: Professional JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Farmington, ME, United States Peacefully nestled in the spectacular lakes & mountains region of western Maine, UMF is Maine’s public liberal arts college, offering quality programs in teacher education, human services and arts and sciences. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. Get ready to launch your coaching career into high gear—the University of Maine at Farmington wants YOU as our new Assistant Alpine Coach for the Men’s and Women’s Teams! This isn’t just a job, it’s a chance to be at the center of the action, where the energy is electric, the mountains are alive, and every day feels like race day. Unleash Your Passion Challenge yourself and our athletes by bringing bold ideas, contagious enthusiasm, and a winning mindset to the most spirited team in Maine. Dive headfirst into brilliant bluebird mornings, epic powder days, and the kind of team camaraderie that makes you want to cheer from the chairlift. Explore every twist and turn of the alpine racing world—from pumping up pre-race adrenaline to leading edge-of-your-seat training sessions, you’ll be the spark that fuels our drive for victory. What You’ll Do Amp up athlete motivation and turbocharge every workout with hands-on coaching and dynamic leadership. Be the creative force behind unforgettable practices, team events, and recruiting adventures—think snow, speed, and serious fun. Tackle travel and logistics like a pro, fueling high-performance results in every run. Who You Are An alpine addict, skier at heart, and ready for a challenge. A communicator who fires up the team and knows how to make every moment on the slopes engaging and memorable. Eager to create a fast-paced, fun-first culture that celebrates diversity, drive, and sportsmanship. Why UMF? UMF is everything a skier could dream of—world-class terrain, fierce competition, and a campus full of energy. Sugarloaf, Titcomb, and Saddleback are your playgrounds, and your athletes are ready to make history. Bring your love of skiing, your wild ideas, and your best coaching game—UMF is where YOU become part of something legendary. Ready to race toward excitement? Apply now and claim your spot at the starting gate—it’s time to make tracks and make memories at UMF! This position is a part-time/temp appointment and pays a $3,000 stipend, prorated based on hire date Typical calendar: October 15 - April 15 Required Qualifications: A high school diploma or equivalent. Experience with sports skills and principles to teach and provide feedback for alpine ski racing Valid driver's license (in good standing, based on UMS standards) Availability to work a flexible schedule that includes days, evenings, and weekends for practices and competitions. Demonstrated professionalism, dependability, and integrity; strong communication and problem-solving skills. Preferred Qualifications: A bachelor's degree. Previous collegiate competitive or coaching experience, particularly in Alpine skiing. Experience with sports recruiting. How to apply: Materials must be submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button below. You will be required to create an applicant profile and application. Additionally, you must upload the following: Cover Letter Resume List of three (3) professional references Important items to know about the recruitment process: Review of applications will begin following the close of business on October 16, 2026 We are not able to consider applicants who require visa sponsorship. Incomplete recruitment materials will not be considered. If materials are received after the recruitment deadline, review will be at the discretion of the university. The successful applicant is subject to appropriate background screenings. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/ . Clery Act The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report . If you have any questions, contact UMF Dept. of Public, Safety / Campus Police, University of Maine at Farmington, 149 Quebec Street, Farmington, Maine 04938-1994 tel 207-778-7400UMF The University of Maine at Farmington has earned a national reputation for excellence, gaining stature as one of the finest state-supported liberal arts colleges in the northeastern U.S. Additionally, UMF is rated 5th in U.S. News & World Report Top Regional Public College North for 2023 and has been rated one of America's Best Colleges by U.S. News 25 times since 1998. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. With enrollment at around 1,600 full-time students, UMF is about the same size as many of New England’s most selective private colleges and offers many of the same advantages, yet at a very affordable price — providing a tremendous college value in a spectacular natural setting. Established in 1864 as Maine’s first public institution of higher education, the University of Maine at Farmington is a founding member of The Council of Public Liberal Arts Colleges (COPLAC) an exclusive national group of public colleges and universities committed to providing superior liberal arts and sciences education. "
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3135": {
      "title": "Audio/Visual Technical Director",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/10/2026 Department: UMF Arts and Humanities Category: Events/Activities JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Farmington, ME, United States Peacefully nestled in the spectacular lakes & mountains region of western Maine, UMF is Maine’s public liberal arts college, offering quality programs in teacher education, human services and arts and sciences. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. The University of Maine at Farmington (UMF) and the Emery Community Arts Center (ECAC) are in search of a full-time, year-round Audio/Visual Technical Director (A/V). The A/V Technical Director at Emery Community Arts Center (ECAC) plays a key role in supporting the technical and organizational aspects of ECAC year-round arts programming. This multifaceted position involves providing comprehensive audiovisual technical support, sound reinforcement, lighting, rigging, event coordination, and stage management for a variety of live events, including performances, concerts, lectures, and other artistic presentations. Additionally, the A/V Technical Director will be responsible for facilitating visual art exhibitions by overseeing gallery preparation, art handling, and installation in ECAC Flex Space Gallery and adjacent lobby areas. The Emery Community Arts Center is a vibrant and versatile arts venue. Our dynamic programming brings local, regional, and national artists, musicians, performers, and scholars to Farmington. Our facility includes: Flex Space is a 1,600-square-foot gallery for traditional exhibits, new media and performance art. Performance Space is a 2,500-square-foot, 120-seat multipurpose black box theater with dynamic vertical foldaway doors that open onto an outdoor performance area. Based on the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant, the annual salary for this position is $45,300.32 plus a 10% employer contribution to the UMS retirement plan. Additional benefits include medical, dental, vision, and tuition waiver programs for employees and dependents. Work Schedule: Due to the event-based nature of the position, the weekly schedule will be irregular, oriented around programming needs and schedule of events, often during evenings and weekends. Working Conditions: Physical requirements include standing for extended periods of time, bending, lifting, climbing ladders, and using stairs and lifts. Lifting and exerting force of more than 50 pounds requires assistance by other employee(s) or mechanical assistance. Individual forces must never exceed 50 pounds. (see job description for physical demands) Essential functions (including but not limited to) Coordinates and manages logistical aspects of events and productions, including venue setup, staffing requirements, implementing technical support, and breaking down events to ensure seamless execution from start to finish. Implements and provides technical assistance in the setup, operation, and troubleshooting of audiovisual, sound, and recording equipment for various events and activities. Ensures the proper functioning and maintenance of all audiovisual equipment, including sound systems, projectors, screens, lighting fixtures, and related accessories to support ECAC events. Hires, trains, manages, and supervises student employee technical crews, art gallery monitors, and student event staff. Creates sound and video design for theatrical productions and performances. Job Description Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Technical Theater or related field and One (1) to three (3) years of professional experience Or a combination of education and experience to equate to a minimum of five (5) years Experience in audio engineering, sound reinforcement, and/or live sound mixing. Experience with professional/theatrical video projection systems including projectors and screens. Application Requirements: Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact information for three (3) professional references We are not able to consider applicants who require any visa sponsorship support Incomplete application materials cannot be considered. Materials received after the initial review date will be reviewed at the discretion of the University. For full consideration, materials must be submitted by 4:30 pm EST on Friday, October 16, 2026 The successful applicant is subject to appropriate background screening and post-offer physical as applicable. The University of Maine at Farmington employees are Mandatory Reporters with the exception of UMF’s licensed, clinical medical providers (including athletic trainers) and mental health providers and their clinical interns when working in their capacity as providers. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/ . Clery Act The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report . If you have any questions, contact UMF Dept. of Public, Safety / Campus Police, University of Maine at Farmington, 149 Quebec Street, Farmington, Maine 04938-1994 tel 207-778-7400UMF The University of Maine at Farmington has earned a national reputation for excellence, gaining stature as one of the finest state-supported liberal arts colleges in the northeastern U.S. Additionally, UMF is rated 5th in U.S. News & World Report Top Regional Public College North for 2023 and has been rated one of America's Best Colleges by U.S. News 25 times since 1998. The campus is in historic downtown Farmington, just a short walk away from coffee shops, funky stores, restaurants, banks, bookstores, a multi-screen movie theater and a whole lot more. Our perfect location combines the active outdoor lifestyle with the arts & smarts of a small college town. With enrollment at around 1,600 full-time students, UMF is about the same size as many of New England’s most selective private colleges and offers many of the same advantages, yet at a very affordable price — providing a tremendous college value in a spectacular natural setting. Established in 1864 as Maine’s first public institution of higher education, the University of Maine at Farmington is a founding member of The Council of Public Liberal Arts Colleges (COPLAC) an exclusive national group of public colleges and universities committed to providing superior liberal arts and sciences education. "
    }
